# vvaharness/util/warn_once.py

One-shot standard-error warnings: a message is printed at most once per key, and the registries of keys can be cleared between repositories.

Source: `vvaharness/util/warn_once.py` (lines 1-94)
Executor: code
Called from: backends and stages that keep a module-level "already warned" set (`vvaharness/util/tokens.py` among them); `reset_warn_once_registries` from the batch orchestrator between repositories

// src: vvaharness/util/warn_once.py:32-39
fn warn_once(seen, key, message):executor=code {
  // one process-wide lock for every set, because some sites run inside the Stage 4 and Stage 6 thread pools
  if (key in seen) return
  add key to seen; console.write(message)
}

// src: vvaharness/util/warn_once.py:42-47
fn stage_label(counter):executor=code {
  prefix = part of counter before the first "_"
  return if (prefix is "s" followed by digits) "[$prefix]" else "[stage]"
}

// src: vvaharness/util/warn_once.py:51-94
fn reset_warn_once_registries():executor=code {
  // abstracted: _REGISTRY_SITES lists 28 (module, attribute) pairs in backends, stages, store and validation (lines 51-83)
  for each (module, attribute) in _REGISTRY_SITES {
    if (module never imported) continue   // never imported means never warned
    if (attribute is a set) clear it in place   // identity preserved
  }
}
